# Atlas Agent Skill Rules

- Keep always-on instructions short and non-contradictory.
- Put long procedures in skills, not root instructions.
- Each skill must have a clear `name` and `description`.
- Skills should be task-specific and auditable.
- Do not include secrets or private credentials in skills.
- Do not create skills that bypass review, tests, permissions, or approval gates.
- Update docs when changing process rules.
- Owner/onboarding skills must point agents to the relevant docs instead of duplicating long architecture sections.
- Project hooks may suggest skills and source-of-truth docs, but must not silently edit files, push branches, post comments, deploy, or bypass approvals.
- New Atlas skills must be added to `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/process/agent-alignment.md`, and `docs/process/file-map.md`.
